Okay, so I’ve officially started planning out the pasture for this new place I’m getting into. It’s a pretty big one – about 5 acres – and I’ve decided to go with a combination of electric and barbed wire. I’ve been looking at a lot of videos online and trying to figure out the best layout, but honestly, I’m feeling a little overwhelmed.  It’s a massive project, and I’m worried about it being too complicated.  I’ve already got a rough idea of where I want the main pathways to go, but I’m struggling with how to actually *install* the fencing.  Do you guys have any experience with this kind of thing?  Any tips on how to avoid mistakes or things that just don’t go smoothly?  I’m hoping to get it done relatively quickly, but I’m also trying to be smart about it.  Any advice would be seriously appreciated!  Seriously, I’m at a point where I just need some real-world perspective.

Also, I’m thinking about adding some brush control – maybe some strategically placed thorny bushes? What’s the best way to do that without completely ruining the pasture?

Thanks!”}”}```python`{
